0 43 146 [
[(Note that the [line~] is always bound to audio block boundaries. This means it always)]
[(starts a ramp in the beginning of an audio block and finishes it at the end of an)]
[(audio block as well. If you want better precision with ramps that are shorter than an)]
[(audio block or ramps that start and stop in the middle of an audio blocks you can use)]
[([vline~], which also has a delay parameter to schedule different ramps.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
